  "summary": "No listed instrument can perform standard bulk crystalline phase identification on ceramic powders. The ideal technique is Powder X-ray Diffraction (PXRD), which is not currently available on the equipment list. As a supplementary option, the transmission electron microscope (EQ11) can be used to acquire selected area electron diffraction (SAED) patterns from individual particles."
}

